{"id":"b515fc72-c72f-48c3-9384-d86d1142e11f","object":"chat.completion","created":1785016633,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    accepted_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        parseable = call.get('parseable', False)\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        norm_tokens = max(1, tokens)\\n        normalized_gain = gain / norm_tokens\\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            'accepted': accepted,\\n            'call_id': call_id,\\n            'normalized_gain': normalized_gain_rounded\\n        })\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted_ids,\\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` for task AGENT-TF-01. The output schema is given: it must return an object with `accepted_call_ids` (list of strings) and `diagnostics` (list of objects with `accepted`, `call_id`, `normalized_gain`).\n\nFrom the prompt: \"For each call subtract loss with the call from loss without it. Normalize gain by at least one prediction token. Require both parseability and normalized gain at or above threshold. Keep diagnostics in supplied call order. Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\"\n\nInterpretation: For each call in `case.calls` (list), compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Then normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens? But \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" Means divide by prediction_to